Package: mica-system
Version: 1.1.0-1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790380800
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: systemd, systemd-sysv, systemd-resolved, systemd-repart, systemd-timesyncd, udev, dbus, passwd, quota, e2fsprogs
Description: Mica OS board-independent system policy
 The system half of every Mica OS root, and of the floor: the DATA layout and
 project quotas, the seed and reconcile tools under /usr/lib/mica with their
 units, the bind mounts of /mica, /mica/containers, /srv, /home, /root, /var,
 /var/lib/mica, /etc/hostname and /usr/local/lib/systemd/system, the health
 gate and the boot-failure handler, the offline provisioning import, the
 default DHCP network, volatile journald storage and the network time policy.
 .
 Enablement is payload: the wants-links and /dev/null masks this package ships
 are the whole of it, and no maintainer script enables a unit. The preset
 50-mica-nftables.preset keeps nftables.service disabled wherever a product
 adds the firewall; the postinst refuses a root in which it is linked.
 .
 SSH and the console are options, not part of this package: mica-ssh carries
 dropbear, and getty@.service and serial-getty@.service start only once the
 console option has installed /usr/bin/login.
 .
 /etc/shadow is built in RAM at every boot from the image's factory copy, every
 account locked; a transient root password set through micad lasts until the
 next boot.
 .
 The postinst creates the operator account mica, uid and gid 1000, home
 /home/mica on DATA, shell /bin/sh, with no supplementary groups and no
 password.
 .
 passwd provides the tools the postinst runs. The verity root needs no
 userspace: the kernel assembles it from the dm-mod.create= table on its
 command line.
